diff --git a/docs/09-frontend-and-pwa.md b/docs/09-frontend-and-pwa.md
index 30c80d62..122c4d62 100644
--- a/docs/09-frontend-and-pwa.md
+++ b/docs/09-frontend-and-pwa.md
@@ -438,7 +438,7 @@ Every form control comes from `components/ui/` and takes its look from the token
 - **Disclosure** (`disclosure.tsx`, #14). A button with `aria-expanded` and `aria-controls` that shows and hides a panel kept mounted while hidden: `variant="box"` is a bordered section whose full-width header is the toggle (a form's Advanced options), `variant="row"` a compact list item header with `actions` beside it. `summary` adds to the toggle's text, `defaultOpen` sets the first state, `open` with `onOpenChange` lets the caller keep the state instead (so it outlives a remount), and `revealDisclosures(element)` opens every collapsed one around an element at once (through `onOpenChange` when the caller keeps it).
 - **Labels, help, required.** `Label required` puts the `RequiredMarker` (an asterisk in the bad tone, `aria-hidden`) after the label, outside the `<label>`, so the accessible name stays the field's name; a control carries `aria-required`. A group (an array, a record, a set of checkboxes) shows the marker after its legend instead, since a group takes no `aria-required`, and states its minimum as text that describes it ("Choose at least 1.", "At least 2 items."); its checkboxes are not each marked. A form with required fields starts with `RequiredNote` ("Required fields are marked \*", hidden from assistive technology, which hears "required" on each control instead). Help text (`HelpText`) is linked to its control with `aria-describedby`.
